hey this is pressure Locker this clock  displays time accurately like any other  12-hour clock but this clock has no  numbers and the clock has been rotated  out of position based on the position of  the hour and minute hands what time is  it this problem appeared as a primary  school math question in China students  were given the multiple choice options  that the time is between 3 &amp; 4 6 &amp; 7 8 &amp;  9 or 10 and 11 can you figure it out  give this problem a try and when you're  ready keep watching the video for the  solution the entire difficulty in this  problem is that the clock is out of  position so we need to orient the clock  how can we do that let's zoom in on the  hour and the minute hands look at the  position of the hour hand it is  four-fifths of the way between one hour  marking and the next hour marking what  does that mean for the minute hand well  the position of the hour hand is  dependent on the position of the minute  hand if the hour hand is four-fifths of  the way to the next hour marking that  means the minute hand is four-fifths of  the way around the clock so the minute  hand is 4/5 times 60 which equals 48  minutes past the hour  therefore the minute hand is between the  hour markings of 9 and 10 and we can  continue numbering clockwise so we can  see the hour hand is past 10 so the hour  will be 10 and we know that the minute  hand is at 48 so we can deduce the time  is 1048 but just for fun let me orient  the clock in the correct position  we can put the 12 at the top and  continue numbering clockwise and we can  see the time is 1048 and that would mean  the correct answer is d the time is  between 10 and 11  did you figure out this problem thanks  for watching this video please subscribe  to my channel I make videos on math you  can catch me on my blog mind your  decisions that you can follow on  Facebook Google+ and patreon you can  catch me on social media at pressure  Locker and if you like this video please  check on my books 